PRE-TABLE BLOCK -- table 15, the v19 L2 REPAIR of {SFRZ set, is_trap} x {MODE, SFD1}.
Written BEFORE table 15's first build, so this file's own mtime proves the order.  2026-09-06.

WHY THERE IS A TABLE AT ALL
  I FILED this cell as clause-(e) DEBT.  Two seats on pass 11 showed it is a FLOOR breach, from two
  independent precedents in this round's OWN records, both verified by opening the artifacts:
    * grok  -- PRETABLE12 graded this EXACT inner `if' L2 ("L2, in-round") when `!is_trap || !(PSR & IND)'
               swept 46/46.  IND, C and SER at this site were then repaired in-round as floor.
    * kimi  -- its VERDICT LINE said DEBT and its BODY reached FLOOR: the pass-5/pass-7 mutants
               `!is_trap || vector == <class>' condition on a field the body does not test either, and
               those were repaired in-round (trapfrozen4/5/6/9, trapfrozen450/496).
  So the repair is in-round and this table is its proof.  minimax said DEBT and is outvoted by ARGUMENT,
  not by count: neither precedent was contested, and both are checkable.

SIBLING PARITY
  The trap side now has five bits that CAN vary: MODE, SFD1, IND, C, SER.  Before v19 three were rowed
  (trapfrozenind, trapfrozenc, trapfrozenser) and two were not.  After v19 all five are.  SFRZ is
  invariant BY CONSTRUCTION -- it is the guard -- and that is stated rather than left as a blank cell.

CLAIM -> ROW
  The contract sentence added by v19 asserts the trap side is closed on all five varying bits.  Rows:
  MODE trapfrozenuser, SFD1 trapfrozensfd1, IND trapfrozenind, C trapfrozenc, SER trapfrozenser.
  No claim is made about multi-axis joints; those stay clause-(e), unchanged.

GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD
  Guard reads PSR (outer) and is_trap (inner).  The guarded body writes `vector = ERROR' and prints the
  re-route diagnostic.  The two new rows put the guard's operand into states no row held.

CHANNEL -- the mutant each row kills and the observable that differs under it
  trapfrozenuser  kills M_RRTRAPMODE (`if (!is_trap || !(PSR & M88K_PSR_MODE))').  TWO observables move
                  together: the row goes from DELIVER at its own vector 0x400 to STOP at 0x50, AND the
                  re-route's diagnostic APPEARS where REFATAL_EXPECT says it must not -> bad=refatal.
  trapfrozensfd1  kills M_RRTRAPSFD1 (the SFD1 twin).  Same two observables, vector 0x38.
  Both channels are already read by the probe; neither row needs new machinery.  A row whose named
  channel cannot vary under its named mutant is vacuous by construction, and these two can.

PREDICTIONS, recorded BEFORE the run so the table can refute them
  BASE                     59/59 before and after; a closing BASE that is not 59/59 VOIDS the table.
  M_RRTRAPMODE   on v19    58/59, killed by trapfrozenuser alone.
  M_RRTRAPSFD1   on v19    58/59, killed by trapfrozensfd1 alone.
  M_RRTRAPMODE   on v17    57/57 -- a CLEAN SWEEP of the pre-repair instrument.  This is the claim that
  M_RRTRAPSFD1   on v17    57/57    makes the repair necessary rather than decorative; if either reds on
                                    v17 then the cell was already covered and the filing was wrong twice.
  CTL_RRTRAPINV  on v19    heavily red (`|| (PSR & MODE)' re-routes ALL sixteen trap rows) -- proves the
                           edit lands at all, the same control shape table 12 used for IND.
  (v18 differs from v17 only in comments, so v17.frozen IS the 57-row instrument.)

